What was taken as published
  Joint origins and axes, joint position limits, effort limits, velocity limits, link masses, centres of
  mass and inertia tensors (from the URDF), and the collision meshes (meshes/collision, unmodified STL).
  KUKA's README marks transformations, all joint limits, inertial values and collision meshes as verified
  for this robot.

What was changed
  Visual meshes: KUKA ships them as Collada (.dae), which MuJoCo cannot read. They were converted to STL
  (meshes/visual) with trimesh, geometry only (KUKA's colours and textures are dropped); vertex positions
  are unchanged, and the URDF visual offsets are carried into each visual geom's pos/quat.
  Inertia tensors: MuJoCo stores them as principal moments with an orientation; the conversion is
  MuJoCo's own URDF compiler, so the values are the same tensors expressed differently.
  The base link's inertia is a placeholder (the base is fixed and its inertia never enters the dynamics).
  Added: a Coral status ring at the base (visual only) and a "flange" site at KUKA's tool0 frame.
